# Copy to .Renviron (which is gitignored) and fill in.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Never commit a real token: a PAT in a commit is
# compromised the moment it is pushed, and GitHub scans for them and revokes
# them for you. .Renviron is in .gitignore for exactly this reason — but note
# that rsconnect DOES include it in a deployment bundle, so the same file
# configures local development and the shinyapps.io deployment.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data sync — persisting what the running app writes (see R/github_sync.R)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these the app works exactly as before: records are written to the
# local filesystem and nowhere else. On a hosted platform that filesystem is
# discarded when the instance recycles, so set these for any deployment whose
# data is meant to survive.
#
# The PAT needs one permission: Contents (read and write) on this repository.
# Create it at https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#
# TMS_GITHUB_REPO_URL=https://github.com/tag-amitkumar/TMS-Transport.git
# TMS_GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# TMS_GITHUB_BRANCH=minimal-setup

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connectors — all optional, all "Not configured" until set
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# TMS_WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# TMS_SENDGRID_KEY=
# TMS_MSG91_KEY=
# TMS_GSP_CLIENT_ID=
# TMS_GSP_SECRET=
# TMS_GPS_API_KEY=
# TMS_RAZORPAY_KEY=
